extends layout

block content
  section.projects
    .container
      h1.section-title Projects

      .projects-grid
        article.project-card
          h3.project-title Personal Website
          p.project-description
            | You're looking at it! This is my digital home—a place to share my work, write about what I'm learning,
            | and make it easy for people to get in touch. It's fast, clean, and feels smooth to navigate.
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | Built with a NestJS backend serving server-rendered Pug templates for SEO benefits. The blog system
              | parses Markdown files with syntax highlighting via highlight.js. Page transitions use the View Transitions API
              | with GSAP animations, while the contact form integrates Zoho Mail OAuth2 with hCaptcha spam protection
              | and XSS sanitisation.
          .project-links
            a.btn(href=`${githubUrl}/jordancolehunt.com`, target="_blank") GitHub
          .tech-stack
            span.tag NestJS
            span.tag TypeScript
            span.tag Pug
            span.tag Vanilla JS
            span.tag Markdown
            span.tag Zoho Mail
            span.tag GSAP
            span.tag highlight.js

        article.project-card
          h3.project-title Lane Racer
          p.project-description
            | A retro-style racing game that runs right in your terminal. Four AI drivers compete to dodge obstacles
            | and cross the finish line first. It's built twice—once in JavaScript, once in Python—as a way to explore
            | how modern features in each language compare when solving the same problem.
            strong  (Work in Progress)
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | Demonstrates feature parity between ES2020+ JavaScript (private fields, generators, Set.difference)
              | and Python 3.10+ (type hints, pattern matching, dataclasses, protocols). Uses the strategy pattern
              | for AI decision-making with full state serialisation, making it ready for LLM or vision model integration.
              | Async/await handles concurrent updates with ANSI terminal rendering at 10 FPS.
          .project-links
            a.btn(href=`${githubUrl}/race-sim`, target="_blank") GitHub
          .tech-stack
            span.tag JavaScript
            span.tag Python
            span.tag Node.js
            span.tag Async/Await
            span.tag Strategy Pattern
            span.tag Terminal UI
            span.tag Generators
            span.tag Type Safety

        article.project-card
          h3.project-title Dino Park
          p.project-description
            | Ever wanted to run a dinosaur park without the risk of being eaten? This simulation lets you manage
            | a grid of enclosures, keeping track of feeding schedules, dinosaur movements, and maintenance alerts.
            | Real-time events keep things unpredictable—just like the real thing, minus the velociraptors.
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | Built with pure functional programming principles in React. Processes real-time events from an external API
              | to manage a 26×16 park grid using immutable data structures throughout. Features a three-panel UI
              | with safety indicators and comprehensive Vitest coverage demonstrating clean functional architecture.
          .project-links
            a.btn(href=`${githubUrl}/dino-park`, target="_blank") GitHub
          .tech-stack
            span.tag React
            span.tag Vite
            span.tag Vitest
            span.tag JavaScript
            span.tag Functional Programming
            span.tag Immutable Data

        article.project-card
          h3.project-title SQL Training Environment
          p.project-description
            | A hands-on SQL training platform built for senior engineering interview prep. Work through progressive
            | exercises—from basic SELECT statements to window functions and CTEs—against real PostgreSQL and SQLite
            | databases. No ORM hand-holding here, just raw SQL and immediate feedback.
            strong  (Work in Progress)
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | Features a unified database abstraction layer that transparently handles PostgreSQL 9.6, PostgreSQL 13,
              | and SQLite through a single interface. Each exercise runs in isolated schemas to prevent data conflicts,
              | with custom Vitest assertions for SQL-specific validation (row counts, column checks, ordering, uniqueness).
              | Docker Compose orchestrates the multi-version PostgreSQL environment.
          .project-links
            a.btn(href=`${githubUrl}/sql-training`, target="_blank") GitHub
          .tech-stack
            span.tag PostgreSQL
            span.tag SQLite
            span.tag Vitest
            span.tag Docker
            span.tag Node.js
            span.tag Raw SQL

      h2.section-title Professional & Client Work
      p.project-description
        | Software I've built and shipped for employers and clients. These repos are private, so
        | there's no GitHub link below — just what each project does, how it's built, and the
        | problem it solved.

      .projects-grid
        article.project-card
          h3.project-title BoyzGroup Odoo AI Assistant
          p.project-description
            | An in-Odoo AI chat assistant that lets non-technical staff ask natural-language questions
            | about live business data—sales, inventory, CRM—and get answers back, including charts,
            | without writing a query.
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | Built as a standard Odoo 17 addon. A question is saved as 'pending' so the request
              | returns fast, then an ir.cron worker runs the actual Claude tool-use loop and pushes
              | the answer back over Odoo's bus channel—no polling. The agent only gets five read-only
              | ORM tools, runs with the requesting user's own permissions, and per-company model
              | blacklists keep it out of data it shouldn't see.
          .tech-stack
            span.tag Python
            span.tag Odoo
            span.tag Anthropic API
            span.tag PostgreSQL
            span.tag OWL

        article.project-card
          h3.project-title BoyzGroup Odoo Integration Server
          p.project-description
            | A webhook-aggregator service bridging Odoo CRM with the outside world: website lead
            | forms, WhatsApp automation, and a phone system, all processed asynchronously.
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | A Fastify server hands every inbound webhook straight to a Redis-backed BullMQ queue
              | rather than processing it inline, so one slow or failing channel can't take the others
              | down. A worker talks to Odoo over JSON-RPC and sends outbound WhatsApp messages through
              | a client interface with a swappable mock implementation, making the whole flow testable
              | without touching a live connection. Deployed on Fly.io.
          .tech-stack
            span.tag TypeScript
            span.tag Fastify
            span.tag BullMQ
            span.tag Redis
            span.tag Prisma
            span.tag Fly.io

        article.project-card
          h3.project-title Acclr8 Pitch Deck Generator
          p.project-description
            | An agent-driven pitch deck build system—Typst source, a shared brand/component template
            | library, and Taskfile-driven rendering—designed to be authored end-to-end by a coding
            | agent rather than a human in a slide editor.
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | Decks are Typst source files importing shared brand/component templates, keeping content
              | and presentation separate. A Taskfile drives the build: one task compiles to PDF, another
              | renders every slide to PNG specifically so a coding agent can visually review its own
              | output and fix layout issues itself.
          .tech-stack
            span.tag Typst
            span.tag Taskfile
            span.tag Claude Code

        article.project-card
          h3.project-title ProForma Generator
          p.project-description
            | A service that generates branded, VAT-correct pro-forma invoice PDFs by combining live
            | courier shipping quotes and customer review data into a single rendered document.
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | Next.js API routes proxy a courier rate API and a reviews API, while a pure business-logic
              | module computes VAT-inclusive/exclusive totals using arbitrary-precision decimal math to
              | avoid floating-point rounding errors in financial figures. The assembled data renders
              | through a React component tree into the final PDF.
          .tech-stack
            span.tag TypeScript
            span.tag Next.js
            span.tag React
            span.tag react-pdf
            span.tag Zod

        article.project-card
          h3.project-title PartsPal
          p.project-description
            | A South African auto-parts marketplace: customers submit a part request with a photo and
            | vehicle details, suppliers respond with competing quotes, and the platform manages the
            | whole request-to-transaction lifecycle.
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | A module-per-domain NestJS app, server-rendered with Pug and small vanilla-JS Web
              | Components. Photo uploads are resized to multiple sizes with a blur placeholder generated
              | in parallel, and can be run through a GPT-4 Vision queue job to help identify the part
              | before a request is even fully filled in.
          .tech-stack
            span.tag TypeScript
            span.tag NestJS
            span.tag Prisma
            span.tag BullMQ
            span.tag GPT-4 Vision

        article.project-card
          h3.project-title Call Center Node Web Server
          p.project-description
            | A NestJS migration of legacy classic-ASP call-center agent tooling—campaign management,
            | lead distribution, dialer integration—moved to a modern stack module by module rather than
            | as a big-bang rewrite.
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | Each feature module follows a consistent controller/service/repository/guard/DTO pattern,
              | exposing both a JSON API and server-rendered views from the same services. A dedicated
              | mocked-services module lets the app run locally without a live database connection,
              | which kept the incremental migration workable day to day.
          .tech-stack
            span.tag TypeScript
            span.tag NestJS
            span.tag MSSQL
            span.tag Pug
